{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJe3EzQH8JTigyXcz9PAex","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n2\t\n3\t> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-16) | 基于 D053 MVP 通过 + Reviewer 建议\n4\t\n5\t## Core Insight\n6\t\n7\tMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。但要训练 agent 学会 selective verification，首先需要解决一个被忽视的训练方法论问题：**step-independent RL 在长 horizon 任务中因 credit assignment decay (gamma^(T-h) → 0) 而灾难性崩溃**。Episode-level training 是前提条件。在此基础上，action-change 作为 intrinsic reward signal 训练 selective verification policy。\n8\t\n9\t## Story Arc\n10\t\n11\t**Dual contribution**: Training methodology + Selective verification system\n12\t\n13\t叙事线：\n14\t1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n15\t2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 是自然方向 → 但现有 step-independent RL 框架在多轮任务上失败\n16\t3. 我们发现根因是 credit assignment decay，提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n17\t4. 在此基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n18\t5. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n19\t\n20\t## Target Venue\n21\t\n22\t待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n23\t\n24\t## Core Claims\n25\t\n26\t### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Episode-level credit assignment is critical for RL training of multi-turn agents\n27\t- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比，不同 h 值的 ablation，mechanistic 分析\n28\t- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n29\t- 强度依据：2x baseline vs catastrophic collapse，机制清晰（gamma^49=7.7%）\n30\t\n31\t### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n32\t- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n33\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n34\t- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n35\t\n36\t### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n37\t- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n38\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n39\t- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n40\t\n41\t## Contingency Plan\n42\t\n43\t如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n44\t- **Plan A**（首选）：paper 变为 pure training methodology contribution — \"Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and How to Fix It\"\n45\t- **Plan B**：加更多 ablation 深挖 episode-level training（context window size sweep, reward shaping, curriculum），做 analysis paper\n46\t- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n47\t\n48\t## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n49\t\n50\t| # | Concern | Severity | Defense Experiment |\n51\t|---|---------|----------|--------------------|\n52\t| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | Context window ablation (h=2,5,10,20,full) 展示 non-trivial threshold + 机制分析 + 展示现有 LLM-agent 工作(RAGEN等)默认 step-independent |\n53\t| 2 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | 加 ScienceWorld / WebShop (if resources permit) |\n54\t| 3 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 加 7B 验证 (if GPU available) |\n55\t| 4 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n56\t| 5 | Selective verification 效果不够 significant | MEDIUM | 多 baseline 对比 (always-on / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold / ARES) |\n57\t| 6 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | 实验直接对比 + 方法论差异表 (SFT router vs RL policy, continuous vs binary) |\n58\t\n59\t## Evidence Status Matrix\n60\t\n61\t| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n62\t|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n63\t| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n64\t| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n65\t| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n66\t\n67\t## Competitive Positioning\n68\t\n69\t| System | Method | ALFWorld | Key Difference |\n70\t|--------|--------|----------|---------------|\n71\t| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n72\t| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token↓ | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n73\t| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n74\t| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n75\t| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default — our baseline |\n76\t\n77\t## Research Phases\n78\t\n79\t1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n80\t2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n81\t3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n82\t4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n83\t5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d90116c-22c6-4950-a8c0-216718955acb","uuid":"37bc09a4-8955-478f-a4c7-a97a75b0d035","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:09:15.758Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n\n> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-16) | 基于 D053 MVP 通过 + Reviewer 建议\n\n## Core Insight\n\nMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。但要训练 agent 学会 selective verification，首先需要解决一个被忽视的训练方法论问题：**step-independent RL 在长 horizon 任务中因 credit assignment decay (gamma^(T-h) → 0) 而灾难性崩溃**。Episode-level training 是前提条件。在此基础上，action-change 作为 intrinsic reward signal 训练 selective verification policy。\n\n## Story Arc\n\n**Dual contribution**: Training methodology + Selective verification system\n\n叙事线：\n1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 是自然方向 → 但现有 step-independent RL 框架在多轮任务上失败\n3. 我们发现根因是 credit assignment decay，提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n4. 在此基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n5. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n\n## Target Venue\n\n待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Episode-level credit assignment is critical for RL training of multi-turn agents\n- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比，不同 h 值的 ablation，mechanistic 分析\n- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n- 强度依据：2x baseline vs catastrophic collapse，机制清晰（gamma^49=7.7%）\n\n### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n\n### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n\n## Contingency Plan\n\n如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n- **Plan A**（首选）：paper 变为 pure training methodology contribution — \"Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and How to Fix It\"\n- **Plan B**：加更多 ablation 深挖 episode-level training（context window size sweep, reward shaping, curriculum），做 analysis paper\n- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n\n## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n\n| # | Concern | Severity | Defense Experiment |\n|---|---------|----------|--------------------|\n| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | Context window ablation (h=2,5,10,20,full) 展示 non-trivial threshold + 机制分析 + 展示现有 LLM-agent 工作(RAGEN等)默认 step-independent |\n| 2 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | 加 ScienceWorld / WebShop (if resources permit) |\n| 3 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 加 7B 验证 (if GPU available) |\n| 4 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n| 5 | Selective verification 效果不够 significant | MEDIUM | 多 baseline 对比 (always-on / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold / ARES) |\n| 6 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | 实验直接对比 + 方法论差异表 (SFT router vs RL policy, continuous vs binary) |\n\n## Evidence Status Matrix\n\n| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n\n## Competitive Positioning\n\n| System | Method | ALFWorld | Key Difference |\n|--------|--------|----------|---------------|\n| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token↓ | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default — our baseline |\n\n## Research Phases\n\n1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JmBPGVKcZHUawbbfhf29At","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data I need. Let me write a comprehensive LaTeX paper based on:\n\n1. The experiment data showing episode-level training vs step-independent (main claim)\n2. The h-sweep ablation\n3. Multi-seed replication\n4. Credit assignment mechanism analysis\n5. Action-change statistics\n6. B-IAVR selective verification\n7. Full verification comparison\n8. No-verify ablation\n9. Entropy-controlled analysis\n10. Causal intervention\n11. Reward signal ablation\n12. ARES comparison\n\n\n13. ScienceWorld transfer\n14. 7B scaling\n15. Per-task breakdown\n\nThe narrative guidance says:\n- 70% training methodology + 30% selective verification\n- Episode-level training is the main contribution (converges to ~36% vs 0% for step-independent)\n- h-sweep shows expected trend with noise\n- Multi-seed variance is moderate (std~4.7pp)\n- Selective verification works but cost-performance tradeoff isn't dramatic (Claim 2+3 as preliminary evidence)\n- Paper leads with episode-level training methodology, selective verification as downstream demo\n- Need to strengthen Phase C ablation to compensate for weaker Phase\n\nI should also incorporate the transfer learning results, scaling experiments with the 7B model, and the per-task performance breakdown to round out the empirical evaluation and demonstrate broader applicability.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14801,"cache_read_input_tokens":24309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14801},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d90116c-22c6-4950-a8c0-216718955acb","uuid":"9707acb3-7da9-497b-888e-7ab201